From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerrod <jerrod.uno@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:55:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] codegen: vpkd3d128 reads a copy of vB when vD == vB

vD is also an input (words outside the packed slot are kept), and the
generated code writes vD piecewise while still reading vB. For an
in-place pack such as `vpkd3d128 v0,v0,5,2,2` the early writes clobber
source bits not yet read, including the float16_4 x sign.

Seen in Crackdown: ~130 in-place sites (mostly sub_826012D0 and
sub_82719CA0) pack the NPC head mesh to float16 every frame; with the
sign lost the heads were drawn ~600 px off screen (RenderDoc capture,
head VB x/y/z all >= 0). With the fix the heads render.

Tests: instr_vpkd3d128.s *_inplace_0 / *_inplace_2.
---
 src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp | 61 +++++++++++++++++++--------------
 tests/ppc/asm/instr_vpkd3d128.s | 14 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp b/src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp
index cbdd7f7..ff0fca9 100644
--- a/src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp
+++ b/src/codegen/builders/vector.cpp
